AWPTCM-T5519 (1.0)  IP directed-broadcast to remote routing
Run date : 2026-09-09      Bench : tb470 (IE520)
Software : IE520-awplus_main-20260905-1714.rel  (AlliedWare Plus, build 09/04/26; bootloader pauld)
Result   : PASS
================================================================================

RESULT
  An off-link (remote) packet destined to a subnet's directed-broadcast address is ROUTED
  from SWITCH_A to the DUT and, with `ip directed-broadcast` on the DUT's target interface,
  delivered as a broadcast onto that subnet.
      directed-broadcast DISABLED on DUT : 0/5  delivered  (dropped - control)
      directed-broadcast ENABLED  on DUT : 10/10 delivered                    => PASS.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED  (two L3 routers, off-link source)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SWITCH_A = u5  S/N 264A23066     DUT = u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0
      source subnet (u5 "vlan4") : vlan50  10.10.50.0/27   (SVI 10.10.50.1)  = sender
      transit link (their "vlan1"): vlan40  10.10.40.0/30   u5 .2 <-> u4 .1
                                    over u5 port2.0.24 <-> u4 port1.0.24
      DUT target subnet (vlan3)  : vlan3   10.10.30.0/27   (SVI 10.10.30.1)
                                   `ip directed-broadcast` enabled
  Receiver = tb470 host eth2.30 = 10.10.30.20/27 on u4 port1.0.2 (tagged vlan3).
  Routing : u5 has  ip route 10.10.30.0/27 10.10.40.1 ;  u4 has  ip route 10.10.50.0/27 10.10.40.2

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA. The "sender behind SWITCH_A" is u5's CPU: u5 sources ICMP from its off-link
  subnet address 10.10.50.1 to the DUT-vlan3 directed-broadcast address 10.10.30.31. The
  packet is routed u5 -> u4 across the /30 transit, then (with ip directed-broadcast) the
  DUT broadcasts it onto vlan3, where the host receives it (captured with tcpdump). A control
  pass with ip directed-broadcast DISABLED shows the packet is dropped. Functional test.

